# DermaIQ - AI Product Image Analyzer

## OpenAI API
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

## Database (PostgreSQL)
# Required for Prisma: set DATABASE_URL, or POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL alone (Vercel/Supabase) — we map it to DATABASE_URL at runtime.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/dermaiq?schema=public"
# Optional: non-pooling URL for migrations; if omitted, DATABASE_URL is used.
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/dermaiq?schema=public"
# POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL="postgresql://..."  # Vercel Postgres pooled — used when DATABASE_URL is unset

## NextAuth (set AUTH_SECRET or NEXTAUTH_SECRET; AUTH_URL or NEXTAUTH_URL for production)
AUTH_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_32
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_32
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

## Google OAuth (Optional - for "Continue with Google")
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id_here
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret_here

## Google Custom Search — product pack images for name search (optional)
# 1. Create a Programmable Search Engine at https://programmablesearchengine.google.com/ (search the entire web).
# 2. Enable Image search in the engine settings and copy the Search engine ID (cx).
# 3. Enable "Custom Search API" in Google Cloud Console and create an API key.
GOOGLE_CUSTOM_SEARCH_API_KEY=your_google_custom_search_api_key
GOOGLE_CUSTOM_SEARCH_CX=your_search_engine_id
# Or use Serper (Google image results, single API key — https://serper.dev):
# SERPER_API_KEY=your_serper_api_key

## Abuse protection (optional — Slack/Discord incoming webhook)
# Alerts when IP or site-wide analyze volume spikes (see lib/security/abuse-alerts.ts).
ABUSE_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/xxx/yyy/zzz
# Public site URL for origin checks (production)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app

## TLS / corporate networks (optional)
# If Vercel CLI or Node shows "unable to get local issuer certificate" behind SSL inspection,
# point Node at your org root CA (do NOT use NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED in production):
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/company-root-ca.pem
